  "step_3": "The decision reason requires considering the sum of all pairwise differences of outcomes. In this case, the only outcome difference is 1000€ (4000 - 3000), and since both lotteries have the same difference, the sum is identical. However, the individual does not mention or compute this sum. Instead, the justification is based on the perceived risk and the idea that the 4000€ outcome is not high enough to justify the 20% chance of getting nothing. This reflects a different reasoning — risk aversion — not the sum of pairwise outcome differences. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason as specified. The information considered (risk and certainty) does not match the required information (sum of outcome differences). The justification also does not follow the rule of the decision reason. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
